# The build context is what `docker build` sends to the daemon before it reads
# a single instruction. Unignored, this repo sends 1.0 GB of it: 650 MB of
# Terraform provider binaries and 321 MB of the dashboard's node_modules,
# neither of which any Go image has ever needed.
#
# The .env exclusion is not about size. A build context is readable by every
# stage, so a secret that gets copied in is a secret in a layer, and a layer
# that is pushed is a secret that is published.

*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/

# Belt and braces: the allowlist above already excludes these, but this file is
# the thing somebody reads when they add a COPY line in a hurry.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/node_modules/
**/.terraform/
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
.git/
